# Mass assignment, NestJS shape. SEC-014 only matches Express req.body /
# Object.assign(_, req.body); in NestJS the body arrives via @Body() and is
# spread into a persisted object. (promoted from the mestjs corpus).
#
# RE2 has no backreferences; anchor on the shape instead of "the same name":
# a @Body() param appears, then within a few lines a spread/assign feeds a
# persistence verb.
id: KEUR-NEST-010
title: Mass assignment — @Body() spread into a persisted object (NestJS)
category: security
severity: error
engine: multiline
window: 14
skip_comments: true
target:
  extensions: .ts
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ node_modules/ dist/ build/ _spec/
patterns:
  - regex: (?s)@Body\(\).{0,400}?(?:create|save|insert|update)\s*\(\s*\{.{0,200}?\.\.\.\s*\(?\s*\w+
    message: "A @Body()-bound object is spread into a create/save/insert/update call — mass assignment (CWE-915): a client can set server-owned fields (role, status, total). Bind a typed DTO and copy allowlisted fields, or use ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true })."
confidence: 0.7
fix: "Accept a DTO with explicit fields + ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true }); never spread the raw body into the entity."
